# nr-relay-pages: the public pages of mixdog-relay (src/pages/{mod,app,connect,update_pc}.rs, assets/pages/, tests/pages.rs).
# Nothing here was compiled (no cargo in this task). No Cargo edge is needed: the pages use regex, serde_json, mixdog-fsio and
# the crate's own js/logline, and the tests tempfile and mixdog-testkit, all already in native/core/crates/mixdog-relay/Cargo.toml.

## 1. native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json
Add the set relay-pages (files: golden.json, record.mjs, extract-assets.mjs) beside the other sets, with the manifest hash the verifier
(benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/verify-manifests.mjs) computes. record.mjs regenerates golden.json from a Node tree:
    node native/core/fixtures/relay-pages/record.mjs <tree>/apps/relay/lib > native/core/fixtures/relay-pages/golden.json
It is run once, before the Node pages are deleted (the byte-equality test then keeps pinning the recorded Node bytes).

## 2. The router (the task that writes the relay's request routing, src/server): what it must call
    use mixdog_relay::pages::{PageReply, PageRequest, app::AppPages, connect::connect_page, update_pc::{is_native_app_request, update_pc_page}};
- At startup, once: `let app = AppPages::load(&config.install_dir);` (reads <install dir>/mobile-release.json, writes the one
  warning line if it is unusable, builds /app and /app/latest.json).
- `/app`: `app.app_page(PageRequest { method, user_agent })`; `/app/latest.json`: `app.latest_release(..)`; `/connect`: `connect_page(..)`.
- The "update your PC" page, where Node calls `isNativeAppRequest(request)` and `sendUpdatePcPage(request, response, details)`:
  `is_native_app_request(user_agent)` and `update_pc_page(method, current, min)`.
- Writing a PageReply: status, then the headers in the order given (they are Node's writeHead order), then the body when Some; a None
  body is `end()` with no data (HEAD, 302, 404, 405). user_agent is the first User-Agent header (Node keeps the first of duplicates).

## 3. mixdog-app-server-daemon compose_flip.rs
Nothing: no protocol method belongs to this task, SERVICE_PENDING is unchanged.

## 4. Later deletion task (the Node pages)
apps/desktop/src/renderer/connect-copy.test.mjs imports sendConnectPage from apps/relay/lib/connect-page.mjs to read the served CSS.
When that Node file is deleted the test must read native/core/crates/mixdog-relay/assets/pages/pairing.css instead (that file is the
shared block, kept contiguous: it is exactly apps/mobile/src/index.html from ".mxp-screen{" to "</style>").
